{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.CategoricalHodgeStarExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.CategoricalHodgeStarExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Structures"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalHodgeStar.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalHodgeStar.exists","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star-exists.lean#L24-L41","doc":"**Existence of the categorical Hodge star.**\n\nOn any object `X` of a category, there exists a `CatHodgeInvolution X`\n(a star morphism `⋆ : X ⟶ X`).  In the Quantum Universe setting\nthe relevant `X` is `Ω^k(A)` and `⋆` lands in `Ω^{n-k}(A)`;\ninvolutivity follows from $S^2 = \\mathrm{id}$ on a commutative\nFrobenius-Hopf algebra. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-hodge-star-exists","label":"prop:categorical-hodge-star-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}